<<.operator-example n:"1" eg:"""[[currentTiddler]getvariable[]]""" ie:"returns the value of the variable ''currentTiddler''">>

The function: `f.getProcText()` will return the body text of the precedure `proc()`

<<.example n:"2" eg:"""\procedure proc()
some text

some more text
\end

\function f.getProcText() [[proc]getvariable[]]

<pre><code><<f.getProcText>></code></pre>"""
>>

The `f.getFnText()` function will also return the body text of `proc()`

<<.example n:"2" eg:"""\procedure proc()
some text

some more text
\end

\function f.fn() [<proc>]

\function f.getFnText() [[f.fn]getvariable[]]

<pre><code><<f.getFnText>></code></pre>
"""
>>

<<.tip """To get the definition of  `f.getFnText()` function we need to use `[[f.fn]getvariable[value]]` in the code below""">>

<<.example n:"2" eg:"""\procedure proc()
some text

some more text
\end

\function f.fn() [<proc>]

\function f.getFnText() [[f.fn]getvariable[value]]

<pre><code><<f.getFnText>></code></pre>
"""
>>
